Q2 - Minimum Meeting Rooms
A company has several meetings scheduled during the same day.
You are given two arrays:
• start[i] represents the starting time of the i-th meeting.
• end [i] represents the ending time of the i-th meeting.
Determine the minimum number of meeting rooms required so that no meeting has to wait.
If one meeting starts at exactly the same time another meeting ends, assume that both meetings require separate rooms.
Return the minimum number of rooms required.
Examples
Input 1:
start = [900, 940, 950, 1100, 1500]
end = [910, 1200, 1120, 1130, 1900]
Output 1:
3
Input 2:
start = [100, 200, 300, 400]
end = [150, 250, 350, 450]
Output 2:
Input 3:
start = [900, 900, 900]
end = [1000, 1000, 1000]
Output 3:
3


def min_meet_rooms(start,end):
    start.sort()
    end.sort()
    i = j = 0
    count = 0
    maxCount = 0
    while i<len(start) and j<len(start):
        if start[i]<=end[j]:
            count+=1
            maxCount = max(count,maxCount)
            i+=1
        else:
            count-=1
            j+=1
    return maxCount

start = [900,940,950,1100,1500]
end = [910,1200,1120,1130,1900]
print(min_meet_rooms(start,end))
